{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/450546-trying-to-introduce-new-players-to-requiem-1e-help-needed","id":450546,"title":"Trying to Introduce New Players to Requiem 1e (Help Needed)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-20T10:04:45-07:00","id":450546,"title":"Trying to Introduce New Players to Requiem 1e (Help Needed)","content":"Okay, my brothers and I have a small Pathfinder group and I'm thinking of introducing them to WoD (either New or Classic, but I'm leaning towards nWoD as it's more crossover-friendly and there is no metaplot), and I want Vampire: The Requiem as the starting point. I want to use Requiem 1e, as that is what I own, using solely the material found in the Requiem and nWoD corebooks from 2004.<br /> <br /> However, how should I best run a campaign for newbie players? Should all five covenants be playable from the start or should they decide on one covenant? Any plot hooks to help me out? I've spent the last few months in a Masquerade mindset and I want to get back into Requiem again. I will be dropping the whole &quot;Vampires are emotionally dead&quot; angle from the game, but that doesn't necessarily mean I'm getting rid of personal horror entirely. I am keeping the Humanity meter, although I will be less stringent with it. I want my chronicle to be an even blend of dark action-adventure, political intrigue, and a little bit of personal horror.<br /> <br /> Any ideas on how to run a starter Requiem game and best introduce it to new players whose only RPG experience is with Pathfinder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 03-20-2015, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T10:15:50-07:00","id":450567,"title":"","content":"I'd use the campaign thing they made for Requiem 1e set in New Orleans, and maybe the New Orleans book itself. Those should be a way to ease them into the setting, considering they're made for newbies.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1459/Vampire-The-Requiem-Demo-Full?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">The Campaign</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2364/City-of-the-Damned-New-Orleans?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">New Orleans</a><br /> <br /> It starts them off immediately and introduces them to concepts as it progresses, so it should provide for a lot of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T10:17:39-07:00","id":450570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/450546-trying-to-introduce-new-players-to-requiem-1e-help-needed?p=450567#post450567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arr